            "text": "An optimal and complete Python program to solve this task:\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n\ndef main():\n    # Load the vectors from disk without modifying the input file\n    vectors = np.load(\"vectors.npy\")\n\n    # Cast to float64 to maintain high numerical precision\n    X = vectors.astype(np.float64)\n\n    # Compute squared norms of each row vector: ||x_i||^2\n    sq_norms = np.sum(X**2, axis=1)\n\n    # Compute pairwise squared Euclidean distances using the identity:\n    # ||x_i - x_j||^2 = ||x_i||^2 + ||x_j||^2 - 2 * <x_i, x_j>\n    dists_sq = X @ X.T\n    dists_sq *= -2.0\n    dists_sq += sq_norms[:, None]\n    dists_sq += sq_norms[None, :]\n\n    # Set exact zeros on diagonal and clamp small negative values from floating-point noise\n    np.fill_diagonal(dists_sq, 0.0)\n    np.maximum(dists_sq, 0.0, out=dists_sq)\n\n    # Compute Euclidean distances\n    dists = np.sqrt(dists_sq, out=dists_sq)\n\n    # Sum all ordered pairs\n    total = np.sum(dists)\n\n    print(f\"TOTAL:{total}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
